{"ts":"2026-07-26T10:28:46.495Z","author":"harness:opencode","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"opencode","op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-cg1sjb"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"SDK entrypoint import-cost gate false-fails on cold filesystem cache: single-shot fresh-process sampling exceeds the 30ms noise margin"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Live reproduction 2026-07-26 on clean main (2026.7.26): the first pnpm lint invocation of the day failed the SDK entrypoint import-cost gate with './sdk/runtime: 545ms > 510ms' (budget 480ms + LATENCY_NOISE_MARGIN_MS 30). An immediate re-run with zero code or environment changes passed all 10 entrypoints, and every subsequent run stayed green. The gate spawns fresh Node processes per entrypoint but takes a single timing sample per check run, so a cold filesystem/module cache on the first run of a session (or a loaded CI runner) converts pure measurement noise into a hard gate failure. False failures train agents to re-run gates until green and erode trust in the pipeline — the symmetric hazard to the false-pass erosion pm-k6t4yb registers. Duplicate check: searched import-cost/noise/cold/flake all-status; pm-38bskj (closed) shaped the entrypoints, pm-ag9nka owns --profile truthfulness, pm-k6t4yb owns the gate registry and negative controls — none own per-run sampling noise of this gate. Fix directions (implementation out of scope for the filing pass): warm-up sample discarded before measurement, min-of-N sampling per entrypoint instead of single-shot, or cache-aware margin; whichever lands must register in the pm-k6t4yb gate registry with a negative-control fixture."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:ci","flake","gate-reliability","performance"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-26T10:28:46.495Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-26T10:28:46.495Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:opencode"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The import-cost gate cannot fail solely because the first sampled process hit a cold cache: measurement uses either a discarded warm-up sample or min-of-N per entrypoint; a simulated cold-cache run is green when costs are within budget; the gate still fails on a genuinely over-budget entrypoint (negative control per pm-k6t4yb); budgets in scripts/bench/sdk-entrypoint-budgets.json are not raised to absorb noise"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-u9d0"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"pnpm lint is deterministic green on main regardless of filesystem cache warmth when entrypoint costs are within budget"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"First cold run failed at 545ms > 510ms on ./sdk/runtime; immediate warm re-runs pass unchanged"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"b7b4ba9231756191b4c2ce5d292063566795697d8dc0f22056f0c145672f0029","message":"Filed from the 2026-07-26 agent-context readiness audit (plan pm-t9e3bc)"}
