{"ts":"2026-08-11T14:34:47.393Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e3bd70efeed1d617d5fc3f49","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"max","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"planner","source":"inferred","confidence":"high","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["focus:pm-doxj","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-doxj","source":"inferred","confidence":"high","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["focus:pm-doxj","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.227","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-11T14:34:47.393Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Sibling instance observed 2026-08-11, cause not determined. token-budget-gate fails locally on health-default (167 estimated tokens against a 137 budget, baseline 496 bytes / 124 tokens) while the hosted Gates (static) job reports 'Token budget gate passed (29 surfaces checked)' on the identical commit 61d68bd7e. The gate measures an isolated PM_PATH fixture, not the real tracker, so no tracker state can explain it: pm health --check-only emits exactly 496 bytes here through both the global binary and node dist/cli.js, and is byte-identical against a copy of the pre-commit tracker. So the divergence is environmental and reproducible locally, not a flake, and it is not the cold-cache timing shape this item owns - nothing here is timed. Recorded as an adjacent instance rather than filed, because the cause was not isolated. Same class as the closed pm-fr4dg8, where a ratchet verdict turned out to be a property of the working copy rather than of the commit, extended to a gate that reads a synthetic fixture. Anyone re-running this locally should trust the hosted verdict and not update the baseline."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-11T14